The new unit of force (F₁) will be F₁ = M₁L₁T₁⁻² = (2M₀)(2L₀)(2T₀)⁻².\nF₁ = (4M₀L₀)(1/4 T₀⁻²) = M₀L₀T₀⁻².\nThus, the new unit of force is equal to the original unit of force. It remains unchanged.
Correct Answer: C

