    "solution": "The formula for the maximum percentage error in a quantity P = (a^x b^y) / (c^z d^w) is given by:\n(ΔP/P) × 100% = |x(Δa/a)| × 100% + |y(Δb/b)| × 100% + |z(Δc/c)| × 100% + |w(Δd/d)| × 100%\n\nGiven: P = (a³b²) / (c√d) = (a³b²) / (c¹d^(1/2))\nPercentage error in a (Δa/a)% = 1%\nPercentage error in b (Δb/b)% = 2%\nPercentage error in c (Δc/c)% = 3%\nPercentage error in d (Δd/d)% = 4%\n\nApplying the formula:\n(ΔP/P) × 100% = |3(Δa/a)|% + |2(Δb/b)|% + |1(Δc/c)|% + |(1/2)(Δd/d)|%\n(ΔP/P) × 100% = 3(1%) + 2(2%) + 1(3%) + (1/2)(4%)\n(ΔP/P) × 100% = 3% + 4% + 3% + 2%\n(ΔP/P) × 100% = 12%\n\nThus, the maximum percentage error in P is 12%.",
