    "solution": "According to the principle of dimensional homogeneity, terms added or subtracted in an equation must have the same dimensions.\n\n1.  From the term (V - b):\n    Since 'b' is subtracted from 'V' (volume), the dimension of 'b' must be the same as the dimension of volume.\n    [b] = [V] = L³\n\n2.  From the term (P + a/V²):\n    Since 'a/V²' is added to 'P' (pressure), the dimension of 'a/V²' must be the same as the dimension of pressure.\n    [a/V²] = [P]\n    So, [a] = [P][V²]\n\n    The dimension of pressure [P] = [Force/Area] = [MLT⁻²/L²] = ML⁻¹T⁻²\n    The dimension of volume [V] = L³\n\n    Substitute these into the expression for [a]:\n    [a] = (ML⁻¹T⁻²)(L³)² = (ML⁻¹T⁻²)(L⁶) = ML⁵T⁻²\n\n3.  Now, find the dimension of the product 'ab':\n    [ab] = [a][b]\n    [ab] = (ML⁵T⁻²)(L³)\n    [ab] = ML⁸T⁻²\n\nTherefore, the dimensions of the product 'ab' are ML⁸T⁻².",
