    "solution": "The dimension of force [F] is MLT⁻².\n\nLet the original units of length, mass, and time be L, M, and T, respectively. The original unit of force is F = MLT⁻².\n\nAccording to the problem:\nNew unit of length L' = L + 0.10L = 1.1L\nNew unit of mass M' = M + 0.20M = 1.2M\nNew unit of time T' = T + 0.30T = 1.3T\n\nThe new unit of force F' in terms of the new units is:\nF' = M'L'(T')⁻²\nF' = (1.2M)(1.1L)(1.3T)⁻²\nF' = (1.2)(1.1)(1.3)⁻² MLT⁻²\nF' = (1.32) / (1.69) MLT⁻²\nF' ≈ 0.781 MLT⁻²\n\nSo, F' ≈ 0.781 F.\n\nTo find the percentage change in the unit of force:\nPercentage Change = ((F' - F) / F) × 100%\nPercentage Change = ((0.781F - F) / F) × 100%\nPercentage Change = (-0.219F / F) × 100%\nPercentage Change = -0.219 × 100% = -21.9%\n\nThis means the unit of force decreases by approximately 21.9%.",
