    "solution": "The Poynting vector S represents power per unit area (energy flux).\nIts dimension should be [Power]/[Area].\n[Power] = [Work/Time] = [ML²T⁻²/T] = ML²T⁻³\n[Area] = L²\nSo, [S] = [ML²T⁻³]/[L²] = MT⁻³.\n\nLet's verify this using the given formula S = (1/μ₀)(E × B):\n1.  Dimension of Electric Field [E]:\n    [E] = [Force/Charge] = [MLT⁻²/AT] = MLT⁻³A⁻¹\n\n2.  Dimension of Magnetic Field [B]:\n    [B] = [Force/(Charge × Velocity)] = [MLT⁻²/(AT × LT⁻¹)] = [MLT⁻²/(AL)] = MT⁻²A⁻¹\n\n3.  Dimension of Permeability of Free Space [μ₀]:\n    We know the speed of light c = 1/√(μ₀ε₀), so μ₀ = 1/(c²ε₀).\n    [c] = LT⁻¹\n    [ε₀] = [M⁻¹L⁻³T⁴A²] (from Coulomb's law F = 1/(4πε₀) q1q2/r²)\n    [μ₀] = 1/[(LT⁻¹)²(M⁻¹L⁻³T⁴A²)] = 1/[L²T⁻²M⁻¹L⁻³T⁴A²] = 1/[M⁻¹L⁻¹T²A²] = MLT⁻²A⁻²\n\n4.  Now, calculate the dimension of S = (1/μ₀)(E × B):\n    [1/μ₀] = M⁻¹L⁻¹T²A²\n    [E × B] = [E][B] = (MLT⁻³A⁻¹)(MT⁻²A⁻¹) = M²LT⁻⁵A⁻²\n\n    [S] = [1/μ₀][E × B] = (M⁻¹L⁻¹T²A²)(M²LT⁻⁵A⁻²)\n    [S] = M^(-1+2) L^(-1+1) T^(2-5) A^(2-2)\n    [S] = M¹L⁰T⁻³A⁰ = MT⁻³\n\nBoth methods yield the same dimension, MT⁻³.",
