    "solution": "The dimensional formula for power (P) is [ML\u00b2T\u207b\u00b3].\nLet the original units be M, L, T.\nThe new units are M' = M/2, L' = 2L, T' = 4T.\n\nNew unit of power P' = [M'L'\u00b2T'\u207b\u00b3]\nP' = [(M/2) (2L)\u00b2 (4T)\u207b\u00b3]\nP' = [(M/2) * (4L\u00b2) * (1/4\u00b3)T\u207b\u00b3]\nP' = [(M/2) * (4L\u00b2) * (1/64)T\u207b\u00b3]\nP' = [ (1/2) * 4 * (1/64) * ML\u00b2T\u207b\u00b3 ]\nP' = [ (4 / 128) * ML\u00b2T\u207b\u00b3 ]\nP' = [ (1 / 32) * ML\u00b2T\u207b\u00b3 ]\nSo, the new unit of power becomes 1/32 times the original unit of power.",
