    "solution": "Let the dimension of mass be [M] = [E\u02e3 v\u02b8 F\u1dbb].\nWe know the base dimensions of E, v, and F:\nDimensions of E = [ML\u00b2T\u207b\u00b2]\nDimensions of v = [LT\u207b\u00b9]\nDimensions of F = [MLT\u207b\u00b2]\n\nSubstitute these into the assumed relation for mass:\n[M\u00b9L\u2070T\u2070] = ([ML\u00b2T\u207b\u00b2])\u02e3 ([LT\u207b\u00b9])\u02b8 ([MLT\u207b\u00b2])\u1dbb\n[M\u00b9L\u2070T\u2070] = [M\u02e3\u207a\u1dbb L\u00b2\u02e3\u207a\u02b8\u207a\u1dbb T\u207b\u00b2\u02e3\u207b\u02b8\u207b\u00b2\u1dbb]\n\nEquating the powers of M, L, and T on both sides:\nFor M: x + z = 1  (Eq 1)\nFor L: 2x + y + z = 0 (Eq 2)\nFor T: -2x - y - 2z = 0 (Eq 3)\n\nFrom (Eq 1), z = 1 - x.\nSubstitute z into (Eq 2): 2x + y + (1 - x) = 0  =>  x + y + 1 = 0  =>  y = -x - 1.\nSubstitute z and y into (Eq 3):\n-2x - (-x - 1) - 2(1 - x) = 0\n-2x + x + 1 - 2 + 2x = 0\nx - 1 = 0\nSo, x = 1.\n\nNow, find y and z:\nz = 1 - x = 1 - 1 = 0.\ny = -x - 1 = -1 - 1 = -2.\n\nThus, the dimensions of mass are [E\u00b9 v\u207b\u00b2 F\u2070] = [E v\u207b\u00b2].",
