    "option_d": "NH3",
    "correct_answer": "C",
    "solution": "Hybridization is determined by the number of sigma bonds and lone pairs around the central atom (steric number).\n\n1.  H2O: Central atom O. 2 sigma bonds (with H), 2 lone pairs. Steric number = 2+2 = 4. Hybridization = sp3.\n2.  CO2: Central atom C. 2 sigma bonds (each double bond has one sigma and one pi bond), 0 lone pairs. Steric number = 2+0 = 2. Hybridization = sp.\n3.  SO2: Central atom S. 2 sigma bonds (each double bond with O has one sigma and one pi bond), 1 lone pair. Steric number = 2+1 = 3. Hybridization = sp2.\n4.  NH3: Central atom N. 3 sigma bonds (with H), 1 lone pair. Steric number = 3+1 = 4. Hybridization = sp3.\n\nTherefore, SO2 has sp2 hybridization at its central atom.",
