    "question": "Which of the following pairs is isostructural?",
    "option_a": "CO2 and SO2",
    "option_b": "PCl3 and BCl3",
    "option_c": "NH3 and BF3",
    "option_d": "XeF2 and I3-",
    "correct_answer": "D",
    "solution": "Isostructural species have the same molecular geometry and hybridization of the central atom.\n\nLet's analyze each pair:\n\n1.  CO2:\n    -   Central atom: C\n    -   Valence electrons: 4\n    -   Bonded atoms: 2 O (double bonds contribute 2 sigma bonds)\n    -   Lone pairs: 0\n    -   Steric number: 2\n    -   Hybridization: sp\n    -   Geometry: Linear\n    SO2:\n    -   Central atom: S\n    -   Valence electrons: 6\n    -   Bonded atoms: 2 O (double bonds contribute 2 sigma bonds)\n    -   Lone pairs: 1\n    -   Steric number: 3\n    -   Hybridization: sp2\n    -   Geometry: Bent (V-shaped)\n    -   Not isostructural.\n\n2.  PCl3:\n    -   Central atom: P\n    -   Valence electrons: 5\n    -   Bonded atoms: 3 Cl\n    -   Lone pairs: 1\n    -   Steric number: 4\n    -   Hybridization: sp3\n    -   Geometry: Trigonal pyramidal\n    BCl3:\n    -   Central atom: B\n    -   Valence electrons: 3\n    -   Bonded atoms: 3 Cl\n    -   Lone pairs: 0\n    -   Steric number: 3\n    -   Hybridization: sp2\n    -   Geometry: Trigonal planar\n    -   Not isostructural.\n\n3.  NH3:\n    -   Central atom: N\n    -   Valence electrons: 5\n    -   Bonded atoms: 3 H\n    -   Lone pairs: 1\n    -   Steric number: 4\n    -   Hybridization: sp3\n    -   Geometry: Trigonal pyramidal\n    BF3: (Analyzed above) Trigonal planar, sp2\n    -   Not isostructural.\n\n4.  XeF2:\n    -   Central atom: Xe\n    -   Valence electrons: 8\n    -   Bonded atoms: 2 F\n    -   Lone pairs: (8-2)/2 = 3\n    -   Steric number: 5\n    -   Hybridization: sp3d\n    -   Geometry: Linear (3 lone pairs occupy equatorial positions, 2 F atoms occupy axial positions).\n    I3- (Triiodide ion):\n    -   Central atom: I\n    -   Valence electrons: 7 (from central I) + 2x7 (from terminal I) + 1 (for negative charge) = 22 total valence electrons. The central I has 7, two terminal I have 7 each, and the -1 charge contributes one more electron. So, 7 from central I. After forming two single bonds with terminal I atoms (2 electrons), 5 electrons remain. Adding the -1 charge makes it 6 lone pair electrons, so 3 lone pairs. (Alternatively, for central atom I: 7 valence electrons. 2 bonds formed with terminal I. Remaining 5 electrons + 1 electron from the negative charge = 6 electrons = 3 lone pairs.)\n    -   Steric number: 2 (bond pairs) + 3 (lone pairs) = 5\n    -   Hybridization: sp3d\n    -   Geometry: Linear (similar to XeF2, 3 lone pairs in equatorial plane, 2 bonded atoms axial).\n    -   Are isostructural.\n\nTherefore, XeF2 and I3- are an isostructural pair.",
