    "solution": "Graphite is an allotrope of carbon with a layered structure.\n\n1.  In graphite, each carbon atom is covalently bonded to three other carbon atoms within the same layer.\n2.  This arrangement results in each carbon atom forming three sigma bonds and having one unhybridized p-orbital perpendicular to the plane of the layer.\n3.  The presence of three sigma bonds around each carbon atom leads to a steric number of 3.\n4.  A steric number of 3 corresponds to sp2 hybridization.\n5.  The unhybridized p-orbitals overlap laterally to form a delocalized pi electron system across the entire layer, which accounts for graphite's electrical conductivity.\n\nTherefore, the carbon atoms in graphite are sp2 hybridized.",
